<p><code>@ueberbit/vite-plugin-drupal</code> turns <a href="https://vite.dev">Vite</a> into a Drupal theme build tool. It bundles your assets, generates the <code>*.libraries.yml</code>, <code>*.breakpoints.yml</code> and a <code>*_dist</code> theme, registers custom elements by file name and gives you HMR for Twig.</p>

{% embed aside with { type: 'tip', title: 'This page is the demo' } %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>These docs are rendered by Drupal with the <code>uebertool_docs</code> theme, which is built with the plugin itself. Every live preview is real Twig, rendered and hydrated in this Drupal site.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

<h2>Install</h2>
<p>Add the plugin and Vite to your theme:</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'sh' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
pnpm add -D @ueberbit/vite-plugin-drupal vite
pnpm add tailwindcss alpinejs vue @vueuse/core morphdom
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

{% embed aside with { type: 'caution', title: 'Install the auto-import presets in your theme' } %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>The auto-import presets are resolved from your theme directory. Without <code>@vueuse/core</code> installed in the theme the build fails with <code>[auto-import] failed to load @vueuse/core</code>.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

<h2>Configure Vite</h2>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'ts', title: 'vite.config.ts' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
import uebertool from '@ueberbit/vite-plugin-drupal'
import { defineConfig } from 'vite'

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    uebertool(),
  ],
})
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

<p>Add the scripts to the theme's <code>package.json</code>. The <code>uebertool</code> binary generates the TypeScript setup in <code>.uebertool/</code> (see <a href="{{ path('uebertool_docs_pages.page', { slug: 'types' }) }}">TypeScript</a>).</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'json', title: 'package.json' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
{
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "uebertool && vite",
    "build": "uebertool && vite build"
  }
}
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

<h2>Wire up the theme</h2>
<p>The build generates a hidden theme called <code>&lt;theme&gt;_dist</code> in <code>dist/</code>. Use it as base theme so Drupal picks up the generated libraries and breakpoints:</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'yaml', title: 'mytheme.info.yml' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
name: My theme
type: theme
base theme: mytheme_dist
core_version_requirement: ^11
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

<p>Then add <code>js/main.ts</code> and <code>css/tailwind.css</code>:</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'css', title: 'css/tailwind.css' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
@import "tailwindcss";
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

<h2>Companion module</h2>
<p>Install <code>uebertool_companion</code> and its submodules alongside the theme. Several features depend on it:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>uebertool_twig_loader</code> attaches the library of a template automatically (<code>templates/foo/foo.ts</code> is attached whenever <code>foo.html.twig</code> renders).</li>
  <li><code>uebertool_cascade_layer</code> wraps Drupal's own CSS in <code>@layer drupal</code>.</li>
  <li><code>uebertool_asset_renderer</code> prevents Drupal from messing with theme assets.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Run it</h2>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'sh' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
pnpm dev    # libraries point to the Vite dev server, Twig HMR enabled
pnpm build  # hashed production assets in dist/
drush cr    # after switching between dev and build
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

<p>Both commands rewrite <code>libraries.yml</code>. Drupal caches library definitions, so clear the cache whenever you switch between <code>dev</code> and <code>build</code>.</p>

{% embed aside %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>In DDEV the dev server URL is taken from <code>DDEV_PRIMARY_URL</code>. Outside of DDEV set <code>UEBERTOOL_URL</code> or the <code>url</code> option.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
